  "observedAt": "2026-10-11T09:09:35.736Z",
  "text": "Feedback\nLanguage: English\nContact Sales \nCreate an AWS Account\nCreate estimate: Configure Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL-Compatible DB\n \nInfo\nDescription\nChoose a location typeInfo\nRegion\nChoose a Region\nUS East (Ohio)\nAurora PostgreSQL-Compatible Edition\nProvides speed and availability of high-end commercial databases with the simplicity and cost-effectiveness of open source databases.\nAurora Serverless PostgreSQL-Compatible Edition\nDatabase capacity automatically scales up or down to meet your application needs.\nAmazon Aurora PostgreSQL Limitless Database\nScales write throughput and storage by distributing a database workload over multiple Aurora writer instances, while maintaining the ability to use it as a single database.\nCluster Configuration Option\nInfo\nAurora PostgreSQL Cluster Configuration Option\nAurora Standard\nCost effective pricing for many applications with moderate I/O usage (I/O costs <25% of total database costs).\nPay-per-request I/O charges apply. DB instance and storage prices don't include I/O usage.\nAurora PostgreSQL Compatible DB instance specifications\nInfo\nQuantity\nEnter the number of DB instances that you need including read replicas.\nSelected Instance:\ndb.r6g.large\nvCPU: 2\nMemory: 16 GiB\nNetwork Performance: Up to 10 Gigabit\nUtilization\nWith utilization, you still have to stop the instance to get the cost benefit. Utilization only affects OnDemand pricing for instances and not the storage, backups, etc.\nValue\nUnit\n%Utilized/Month\nPricing model\nOnDemand\nShow calculations\nRDS Proxy\nInfo\nWould you be creating an RDS Proxy with the database?\nYes\nShow calculations\nDatabase Storage\nInfo\nStorage amount\nTotal Storage Size of the Aurora Cluster\nValue\nUnit\nGB\nBaseline IO rate\nEnter the number of IOs per second that your workload consumes during off-peak periods.\nValue\nUnit\nper second\nPeak IO rate\nEnter the maximum number of IOs per second your workload consumes during peak periods.\nValue\nUnit\nper second\nDuration of peak IO activity\nEnter the number of hours per month when your cluster or instance workload operates at peak.\nValue\nUnit\nhours per month\nShow calculations\nCloudWatch Database Insights Pricing for RDS Provisioned Instances\nInfo\nWould you be enabling Database Insights with the database?\nYes\nShow calculations\nRDS Extended Support\nInfo\nNote: You will not be charged for RDS Extended Support until the Extended Support pricing start date for your database major version. To check the pricing start date for your engine, please refer to the Aurora PostgreSQL user guide.\nDo you plan on running an Extended Support major version (PostgreSQL 11 or higher)?\nYes\nPlease choose the pricing year for RDS Extended Support (Pricing in year 3 is higher than the pricing in the first 2 years)\nYear 1 and Year 2 cost\nNumber of hours running on Amazon RDS Extended Support\nUnit\nper month\nShow calculations\nBackup Storage\nInfo\nSnapshot Export\nInfo\nAcknowledgement\nAWS Pricing Calculator provides only an estimate of your AWS fees and doesn't include any taxes that might apply. Your actual fees depend on a variety of factors, including your actual usage of AWS services.Learn more \n\n\n\nTotal Upfront cost: 0.00 USD\nTotal Monthly cost: 229.95 USD\nShow Details\nCancel\nSave and view summary\nSave and add service\nPrivacy\nSite terms\nCookie preferences\n© 2026, Amazon Web Services, Inc. or its affiliates. All rights reserved.",
